### Tested versions

Reproductible in: v4.7.dev5.official [a8643700c]

### System information

Godot v4.7.dev5 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060 6GB (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8157) - AMD Ryzen 7 2700X Eight-Core Processor (16 threads) - 15.94 Gio memory

### Issue description

Modifying the UVs on post-processing shader (with decimal values) results in a linear rendering, whereas it works correctly in Forward mode.
<img width="728" height="268" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/29eb206b-8c5e-4e78-9830-358e8cb4f455" />
I saw that the problem (or similar problems) had been discussed in different places, but without finding a solution, I'm not sure if we can call it a bug, but I was wondering if there was a solution to work around it currently.


### Steps to reproduce

The MRP is configured in compatibility mode, simply run the scene to see the linear rendering caused by the post-processing effect.

The post-processing shader:
```
shader_type canvas_item;

uniform sampler2D screen_texture:hint_screen_texture,filter_nearest_mipmap;

void fragment() {
	vec2 uv = SCREEN_UV;
	uv.x += sin((uv.y*20.0)+TIME)/100.0;
	vec4 color = textureLod(screen_texture,uv,0.0);
	COLOR = color;
}
```

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

[post-processing-compatibility.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26982114/post-processing-compatibility.zip)
